    "result_text": "The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec: on a successful owner create, emit an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger containing the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Changes made**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (one small function class per step, wired in YAML):\n\n1. **New step `AuditOwnerCreated`** (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`) \u2014 reads the saved `@Val Owner` and logs via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` an info line carrying `owner.getId()`, `owner.getCustomerCode()`, and `owner.getRegistrationDate()`.\n\n2. **Wired it into `owners.POST.yml`** between `save` and `respond` (`save.next: audit`, `audit.next: respond`), under the same `transaction` governance. Placing it after `SaveOwner` guarantees the owner has its generated id; the values are already set upstream by `AssignCustomerCode` and `BuildOwner`/`ResolveRegistrationDate`.\n\n**Results:**\n- Target test `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes \u2014 the log confirms it: `AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-17`.\n- Full `./mvnw test`: **BUILD SUCCESS**, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.\n\n`registrationDate` is logged via `LocalDate.toString()` (ISO `yyyy-MM-dd`), which matches the JSON `registrationDate` the test asserts against.",
